WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
In the mid-Ming dynasty, Japanese pirates often raided the southeastern coast, and the people felt very uneasy.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.800
The fishermen gathered up their nets and watched the dark shapes on the sea with worry.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:16.000
The young general Qi Jiguang came to Zhejiang, determined to defend the coastal frontier.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.400
People lined the streets to welcome him, and children waved their little hands and cheered.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:24.600
He recruited new soldiers and built the strictly disciplined Qi Family Army.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:29.200
The new soldiers stood straight and tall, their eyes full of hope and determination.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:34.200
On the seaside training ground, the soldiers practiced the Mandarin Duck formation, working together in perfect unison.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:39.200
They practiced again and again; their movements grew neater and their teamwork better and better.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:43.200
The Qi Family Army fought many battles in Zhejiang and Fujian, gradually putting an end to the pirate menace.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:48.200
The troops crossed mountains and ridges, their red banners fluttering in the sea wind.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:52.200
Peace returned to the coast; fishing boats went out to sea, and the people lived and worked in contentment.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:57.200
The fishermen sang as they cast their nets, and children ran happily along the beach.
